{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone","id":1387826,"title":"What action movie sequence should have killed/ seriously injured someone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T16:13:25-07:00","id":1387826,"title":"What action movie sequence should have killed/ seriously injured someone?","content":"I'm talking things like leaping off buildings, grabbing a ledge while falling, or taking on beatings which should have sent a person to the hospital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T17:23:28-07:00","id":1387839,"title":"","content":"After reading your question, I was reminded of the scene in Terminator where the T-800 goes to the gun store and the gun owner asks him which gun he'd like to purchase and Arnold responds with &quot;all.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T17:25:20-07:00","id":1387840,"title":"","content":"I think the list of action movies that don't downplay how dangerous things are would be significantly faster to establish.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I can't think of any unless &quot;superpowers&quot; can handwave things that don't make sense (like the number of people that should be dead from Superman catching them while falling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T17:59:08-07:00","id":1387847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone?p=1387840#post1387840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the list of action movies that don't downplay how dangerous things are would be significantly faster to establish.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I can't think of any unless &quot;superpowers&quot; can handwave things that don't make sense (like the number of people that should be dead from Superman catching them while falling).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then I guess I should change the title. <br /> <br /> I'm writing a story, and I&quot;m trying to draw in contrasts between the 'real' world, and the world of 'exalted'. Basically, I'm searching for examples where Exalted do things that would cripple a normal person, and I want to specifically draw attention on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:48:47-07:00","id":1387860,"title":"","content":"But the problem largely isn't the &quot;worlds&quot; in question (though Creation is more forgiving than reality in general).<br /> <br /> Exalted do things that would kill or cripple a normal person in their own setting, because they have superpowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T19:40:42-07:00","id":1387871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone?p=1387860#post1387860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the problem largely isn't the &quot;worlds&quot; in question (though Creation is more forgiving than reality in general).<br /> <br /> Exalted do things that would kill or cripple a normal person in their own setting, because they have superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I&quot;m talking about the low-key superpowers that people don't usually see, and that people don't usually notice. It's so that I can both put in realism and really showcase superhumanity in more subtle ways than 'whoo, I'm glowing!'. <br /> <br /> Like, say, being able to jump through windows without getting horribly cut. Or being able to walk off stab wounds to the abdomen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T19:50:28-07:00","id":1387872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone?p=1387847#post1387847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, then I guess I should change the title.<br /> <br /> I'm writing a story, and I&quot;m trying to draw in contrasts between the 'real' world, and the world of 'exalted'. Basically, I'm searching for examples where Exalted do things that would cripple a normal person, and I want to specifically draw attention on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon reading the title, and especially this, I think of the Matrix. Pretty much every real action sequence in it that involves bullets.<br /> <br /> Granted, there may be people out there getting superpowers from getting shot by bullets but if so they're hiding very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:35:18-07:00","id":1387896,"title":"","content":"Pretty much the last half of The Raid: Redemption and most of its sequel have amazing fights but how the protagonist is still living afterwards is a question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T18:46:09-08:00","id":1474941,"title":"","content":"This is answered by basically anything in the Raid films. Any sequence should've either killed or at the very least severely incapacitated someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26060-nuhxnger36","name":"NuHxnger36","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T15:39:04-07:00","id":1479447,"title":"","content":"The fight scene in The Hunted with Tommy Lee Jones &amp; Benito El Torino. That final fight lasted longer then it should when it involved two expert knife fighters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:30:26-07:00","id":1480616,"title":"","content":"I think bad guys should be punished and good people get good results, but sometimes filmmakers don't think so, I watched movies on android app <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">inat tv pro modsuper.com</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27412,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27412-domingogarner","user":"DomingoGarner","date":". 05-10-2022, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27412-domingogarner","name":"DomingoGarner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T10:01:34-07:00","id":1481088,"title":"","content":"When Joker fell in the Dark Knight and he gets saved by a bat line. Shouldn't the sudden stop broke some of the Joker's bones at least?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T11:29:51-07:00","id":1481098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone?p=1481088#post1481088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Joker fell in the Dark Knight and he gets saved by a bat line. Shouldn't the sudden stop broke some of the Joker's bones at least?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to notice because of the camera angle, but it isn't actually a sudden stop, there's almost a second between the line starting to slow Joker and him coming to a full stop. That would be enough to disperse energy more safely, not as nicely as in the movie, but no breaking bones.<br /> <br /> The ankle also resists this stress better than the neck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T11:54:45-07:00","id":1481385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1387826-what-action-movie-sequence-should-have-killed-seriously-injured-someone?p=1481098#post1481098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to notice because of the camera angle, but it isn't actually a sudden stop, there's almost a second between the line starting to slow Joker and him coming to a full stop. That would be enough to disperse energy more safely, not as nicely as in the movie, but no breaking bones.<br /> <br /> The ankle also resists this stress better than the neck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take your word on that matter. It's been awhile since I watched the film and looked at the camera angles. I just remember that the Joker fell a fair distance before Batman was able to roll into position and deploy the batline to save The Joker's life. I thought he should have broken angle among other things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":""